From 6fc6e1844ed4f884923e2d7575fd4faaade88b0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:31:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi: Bluetooth starts 1 s after UFS (sweetbtdelay default 1):
 Control Center's Bluetooth button

With the controller up only after 30 s, bluetoothd exited four times first and SpringBoard never
opened its MobileBluetooth session: no Bluetooth button in Control Center. With sweetbtdelay=1
(boot 0236b) SpringBoard attaches and the button is there (user).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c
index a5beccc..3e0c025 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c
@@ -1,8 +1,10 @@
 /*
  * umi Bluetooth: the Bluetooth side of the QCA6390 -- the Wi-Fi's chip -- on the UART of QUP
  * serial engine 6 (HCI over H4). Nothing runs unless boot-arg sweetbt=N asks for steps 1..N; they
- * run in a thread of their own, sweetbtdelay seconds (default 30: after the Wi-Fi thread has voted
- * the chip's shared rails) after sweet_ufs_init() starts it.
+ * run in a thread of their own, sweetbtdelay seconds (default 1) after sweet_ufs_init() starts it:
+ * the controller must be up before bluetoothd and SpringBoard start. With 30 s, bluetoothd exited
+ * four times first and SpringBoard's Bluetooth client never came back: no Bluetooth button in
+ * Control Center (umi boots 0236 / 0236b).
  *
  * Adapted from project-BadApple (github.com/aTechGeekDev/ios-apollo, xnu 0136, 0137, 0141, 0143,
  * 0145: bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c; MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Leo Malik, dipa-studio), itself ported from
@@ -126,7 +128,7 @@ void sweet_bt_init(void);
 #define BT_NVM_MOST     16384u
 #define BT_PATCH_MOST   (512u * 1024u)
 
-static uint32_t bt_steps, bt_delay = 30, bt_swctrl_drive;
+static uint32_t bt_steps, bt_delay = 1, bt_swctrl_drive;
 static uint32_t bt_baud = 921600;
 static const struct sweet_bt_speed *bt_want;                    /* sweetbtbaud */
 static const struct sweet_bt_speed *bt_speed = &sweet_bt_speeds[0];     /* what the UART runs at */
-- 
